## ✅ Simplest Merge Sort Code in C

```c
#include <stdio.h>

// 🔹 Merges two sorted halves into one sorted array
void merge(int arr[], int l, int m, int r) {
    int i = l;       // Starting index of left half
    int j = m + 1;   // Starting index of right half
    int k = 0;

    int temp[100];   // Temp array (large enough for demo)

    // Compare and copy smaller elements from both halves
    while (i <= m && j <= r) {
        if (arr[i] < arr[j])
            temp[k++] = arr[i++];
        else
            temp[k++] = arr[j++];
    }

    // Copy remaining elements of left half (if any)
    while (i <= m)
        temp[k++] = arr[i++];

    // Copy remaining elements of right half (if any)
    while (j <= r)
        temp[k++] = arr[j++];

    // Copy temp[] back into arr[]
    for (i = 0; i < k; i++)
        arr[l + i] = temp[i];
}

// 🔹 Recursively divides and sorts the array
void mergeSort(int arr[], int l, int r) {
    if (l < r) {
        int m = (l + r) / 2;

        // Sort first half
        mergeSort(arr, l, m);

        // Sort second half
        mergeSort(arr, m + 1, r);

        // Merge sorted halves
        merge(arr, l, m, r);
    }
}

// 🔹 Print the array
void printArray(int arr[], int n) {
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
        printf("%d ", arr[i]);
    printf("\n");
}

// 🔹 Main function
int main() {
    int arr[] = {5, 2, 4, 6, 1, 3};
    int n = sizeof(arr) / sizeof(arr[0]);

    printf("Original array: ");
    printArray(arr, n);

    mergeSort(arr, 0, n - 1);

    printf("Sorted array: ");
    printArray(arr, n);

    return 0;
}
```

---

## 🧠 Explanation (Breakdown)

### 🧩 `mergeSort(arr, l, r)`
- Base case: If array has 1 element → it's already sorted.
- Recursive case:  
  1. Find middle: `m = (l + r)/2`
  2. Sort left half: `mergeSort(arr, l, m)`
  3. Sort right half: `mergeSort(arr, m+1, r)`
  4. Merge the two sorted halves.

---

### 🧩 `merge(arr, l, m, r)`
- You have two sorted parts:
  - Left: `arr[l..m]`
  - Right: `arr[m+1..r]`
- Merge them into a temporary array.
- Then copy that back into original array.

